{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "11", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "10", "M": "39", "S": "50"}}, "news": [{"title": "Telangana opens doors for homestays, to invite families into tourism economy", "para": "Telangana is launching a new homestay scheme for homeowners to host tourists. This initiative aims to boost tourism beyond major cities and hotels. Eligible properties include independent houses and traditional dwellings across the state. The government will act as a facilitator, promoting community-based tourism experiences. This policy is part of Telangana's broader tourism development plan.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/hospitality/telangana-opens-doors-for-homestays-to-invite-families-into-tourism-economy/133144131?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-198586/133144131.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "hospitality"}, {"title": "Chandigarh housing board residents face regulatory challenges due to frequent policy changes", "para": "Residents of the Chandigarh Housing Board are grappling with regulatory hurdles stemming from frequent policy changes. With previous constructions retroactively classified as violations, they face considerable distress. Many express that the retrospective application of new regulations imposes unfair burdens and legal issues. The Board is aware of these challenges and is actively developing a new, need-based policy aimed at providing clarity and safeguarding homeowner rights.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/chandigarh-housing-board-residents-face-regulatory-challenges-due-to-frequent-policy-changes/133144092?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-36434/133144092.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "New walls, gates and farmhouses come up again in protected Aravalis", "para": "Construction remains unabated at Ansal Aravali Retreat within the protected hills of Raisina, as a recent inspection revealed over two dozen active sites. This development is occurring despite ongoing proceedings with the National Green Tribunal and previous orders for restoration. The area is governed by strict laws banning unauthorized construction and tree removal.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/new-walls-gates-and-farmhouses-come-up-again-in-protected-aravalis/133144044?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-269526/133144044.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}